#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:9
msgid "Launching nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:11
msgid "**Goal:** Use a command line tool to launch multiple nodes at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:13
msgid "**Tutorial Level:** Beginner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:15
msgid "**Time:** 5 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:19
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:22
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:24
msgid ""
"In most of the introductory tutorials, you have been opening new terminals "
"for every new node you run. As you create more complex systems with more and "
"more nodes running simultaneously, opening terminals and reentering "
"configuration details becomes tedious."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:27
msgid ""
"Launch files allow you to start up and configure a number of executables "
"containing ROS 2 nodes simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:29
msgid ""
"Running a single launch file with the ``ros2 launch`` command will start up "
"your entire system - all nodes and their configurations - at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:32
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:34
msgid ""
"Before starting these tutorials, install ROS 2 by following the instructions "
"on the ROS 2 :doc:`../../../../Get-Started/Installation` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:36
msgid ""
"The commands used in this tutorial assume you followed the binary packages "
"installation guide for your operating system (deb packages for Linux). You "
"can still follow along if you built from source, but the path to your setup "
"files will likely be different. You also won't be able to use the ``sudo apt "
"install ros-<distro>-<package>`` command (used frequently in the beginner "
"level tutorials) if you install from source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:40
msgid ""
"If you are using Linux and are not already familiar with the shell, `this "
"tutorial <https://www.linux.com/training-tutorials/bash-101-working-cli/>`__ "
"will help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:42
msgid ""
"As always, don't forget to source ROS 2 in :doc:`every new terminal you open "
"<../../../../Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:45
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:48
msgid "Running a Launch File"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:50
msgid "Open a new terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:52
msgid "$ ros2 launch turtlesim multisim.launch.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:56
msgid "This command will run the following launch file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:58
msgid ""
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"import launch_ros.actions\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    return LaunchDescription([\n"
"        launch_ros.actions.Node(\n"
"            namespace='turtlesim1', package='turtlesim',\n"
"            executable='turtlesim_node', output='screen'),\n"
"        launch_ros.actions.Node(\n"
"            namespace='turtlesim2', package='turtlesim',\n"
"            executable='turtlesim_node', output='screen'),\n"
"    ])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:63
msgid ""
"The launch file above is written in Python, but you can also use XML and "
"YAML to create launch files. You can see a comparison of these different ROS "
"2 launch formats in :doc:`../../../../Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-file-"
"different-formats`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:66
msgid "This will run two turtlesim nodes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:70
msgid ""
"For now, don't worry about the contents of this launch file. You can find "
"more information on ROS 2 launch in the :doc:`ROS 2 launch tutorials "
"<../../../../Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-Main>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:74
msgid "(Optional) Control the Turtlesim Nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:76
msgid ""
"Now that these nodes are running, you can control them like any other ROS 2 "
"nodes. For example, you can make the turtles drive in opposite directions by "
"opening up two additional terminals and running the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:79
msgid "In the second terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:81
msgid ""
"$ ros2 topic pub  /turtlesim1/turtle1/cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "
"\"{linear: {x: 2.0, y: 0.0, z: 0.0}, angular: {x: 0.0, y: 0.0, z: 1.8}}\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:85
msgid "In the third terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:87
msgid ""
"$ ros2 topic pub  /turtlesim2/turtle1/cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "
"\"{linear: {x: 2.0, y: 0.0, z: 0.0}, angular: {x: 0.0, y: 0.0, z: -1.8}}\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:91
msgid ""
"After running these commands, you should see something like the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:96
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:98
msgid ""
"The significance of what you've done so far is that you've run two turtlesim "
"nodes with one command. Once you learn to write your own launch files, "
"you'll be able to run multiple nodes - and set up their configuration - in a "
"similar way, with the ``ros2 launch`` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes.rst:101
msgid ""
"For more tutorials on ROS 2 launch files, see the :doc:`main launch file "
"tutorial page <../../../../Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-Main>`."
msgstr ""

